   "text": "I read the structure region by region and wrote it as the SMILES below. The stereocentres were assigned by hand from the wedges and hashes, not checked with software.\n\n**Fragments**\n- **Aryl ether:** a 3-chloro-4-cyanophenyl group, bonded through O to a cyclobutane.\n- **Tetramethylcyclobutane:** one ring carbon carries the aryl ether O (wedge). The adjacent CMe2 sits on one side, and the other CMe2 sits between this carbon and the NH-bearing carbon (hashed NH bond).\n- **Benzamide:** the NH forms an amide to a para-substituted benzene, whose para position carries an azetidine nitrogen.\n- **Azetidine side chain:** the azetidine C3 carries a CH2 that leads to an N-isopropyl tertiary amine.\n- **Aminocyclobutane:** the tertiary amine is bonded (wedge) to a 1,3-disubstituted cyclobutane, whose other carbon carries an O (hash).\n- **Phthalimide end:** that O is attached to the 5-position of an isoindoline-1,3-dione. Its ring N carries a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group, drawn with no stereo.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- The two cyclobutane stereocentres bearing O and NH on the tetramethylcyclobutane are set from the wedge and hash drawn at each.\n- On the aminocyclobutane, the N is wedged and the O is hashed, which makes it a trans-1,3 arrangement. I assigned both centres as `@` in the SMILES order used.\n- The glutarimide carbon has no wedge, so it is left unspecified.\n\nSMILES: N#Cc1ccc(O[C@H]2C(C)(C)[C@H](NC(=O)c3ccc(N4CC(CN(C(C)C)[C@H]5C[C@H](Oc6ccc7C(=O)N(C8CCC(=O)NC8=O)C(=O)c7c6)C5)C4)cc3)C2(C)C)cc1Cl"
